      "lineNbr": 172,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-05T08:51:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I want to call the callbacks only if the policy effect changed. The logic is\n\nif it\u0027s an old device \u003d\u003e do nothing; actually might be a bug since the device is found twice.\nif it\u0027s a new device \u003d\u003e tell the client that the device effect is None, it should be changed once the SDP is done and on_remote_device_properties_changed should be called.\n\nIf we don\u0027t want the callback in here, clients will need to call GetDevicePolicyEffect on every new device or just assume it\u0027s None. I think both ways are ok for me.",
      "parentUuid": "d261ab49_af861961",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 167,
        "startChar": 76,
